    {
      "claim": "Class: incomplete-item. Where: metasystem/internal/steward/claim_quota.go. If the holding goal has a unit that is settled but not 'collected and published', the claim-quota ask is withheld for the whole blocking interval. That covers a dropped unit, a dropped goal-branch commit, and a commit whose reads are waived and is ready to land. Such a goal has no work in flight, and this is exactly when the goal's Intent and design D13 require the holder to be asked once. The in-flight gate is an allow-list of three stage prefixes and treats every other stage as busy, including these settled ones. As a result a goal that once dropped a unit is never asked to release the machine's one claim again, while ready priority-1 work waits behind it. The page shows only 'not yet asked'. Change: treat the settled stages as not in flight, either by adding the 'dropped' prefix and 'committed, ready to land without a read' to the settled set, or better by listing the stages that really are in flight (starting, running, built or committed ready for review, under examination, collected but not yet published, drop pending, stopped needing a revision). Add those stages to TestNoReleaseIsProposedForWorkInFlight's expect-an-ask cases.",
      "evidence": "Traced path in the reviewed tree. (1) claim_quota.go:166-170: claimQuotaInFlight returns true for any stage not starting with 'reviewed; its read is collected and published', 'stopped:' or 'transferred'. (2) The production reader (cmd/metasystem/steward_seat.go:246-258, then intent_selection.go:147-208) returns workStage and manualWorkItem.stage strings. A dropped named unit reads 'dropped' or 'dropped; prior reads retained' (intent_selection.go:69-77 with board/card.go:160-169). A dropped goal-branch commit reads 'dropped; prior reads retained' (intent_selection.go:330-332). A reads-waived commit reads 'committed, ready to land without a read' (intent_selection.go:346-347). (3) claim_quota.go:259-262: when busy, the ask loop appends a nil error and continues, so askOnce never runs. The next tick reads the same stage, so the ask never comes for that occurrence or for any later occurrence while the stage lasts. (4) unit_boundary.go:131-133 in the same package already counts 'committed, ready to land without a read' as completed, so the two readers disagree. The unit's own test (claim_quota_test.go:383-389) checks only in-flight stages and the published stage, never a dropped or reads-waived one. On R-124 (a finding is material only if the slice does not work or is not safe without the fix): the slice's one deliverable, asking the holder once per blocking interval, does not happen for these goals, so the slice does not work for them.",
